# StickLab OS package list — coding + learn-Linux + 3 Wayland desktops + GPU, budgeted <2GB USB image.
# GPU: NVIDIA (open modules + userspace = CUDA-ready) + AMD/Intel Vulkan + OpenCL loader.
# Languages pre-installed: C/C++, Python, Go, Node, Rust (via rustup), Java-runtime, Ruby, PHP, Lua, Perl.
# Full JDK / CUDA toolkit install on demand via `sticklab setup-gpu` / pacman (online).

# --- base system ---
base
linux
linux-firmware
intel-ucode
amd-ucode
sof-firmware
systemd
systemd-sysvcompat
pacman
glibc
bash
coreutils
shadow
sudo

# --- shells + editors (choice, not opinionated) ---
nano
neovim
zsh
zsh-autosuggestions
zsh-syntax-highlighting
tmux

# --- coding toolchains (pre-downloaded) ---
gcc
make
pkgconf
patch
git
python
python-pip
# NOTE: `rust` and `rustup` conflict — pacman silently drops `rust`. We ship
# `rustup` (multi-toolchain + MCU targets); first toolchain is one command away:
# `rustup toolchain install stable`. So `rustc`/`cargo` show as pending in
# `sticklab langs` until then — by design, not a missing package.
go
rustup
nodejs
sqlite
ruby
php
lua
perl
jre-openjdk-headless

# --- GPU: NVIDIA CUDA-ready + AMD/Intel + OpenCL ---
nvidia-open
nvidia-utils
vulkan-icd-loader
vulkan-intel
vulkan-radeon
vulkan-nouveau
ocl-icd

# --- CLI power tools + learn-Linux kit ---
htop
btop
eza
bat
fzf
ripgrep
fd
tree
ncdu
jq
strace
lsof
file
unzip
zip
iproute2
iputils
openssh
man-db
man-pages
tealdeer
curl
wget
gnupg
github-cli
just
cmake
ninja

# --- hardware bench: MCU / embedded coders (Arduino, ESP32, STM32, Pico, AVR) ---
# Offline on the ISO: serial console, flashing, debug, I2C, logic capture.
# Heavy compilers (ARM/AVR GCC, Arduino-CLI, esptool) stay one command away:
# `sticklab setup-hardware` (2GB budget). Detect boards with `sticklab boards`.
picocom
openocd
avrdude
dfu-util
i2c-tools
sigrok-cli

# --- hardware + networking (run on every PC) ---
networkmanager
iwd
usbutils
pciutils
bluez
bluez-utils

# --- desktop: 3 Wayland compositors (stacking + tiling + dynamic) + shared helpers ---
# labwc = stacking default (Openbox-style) · sway = manual tiling · hyprland = dynamic tiling + eye candy.
# All three share waybar / wofi / foot / mako / swaybg, same Bolt(=Alt) keys, same lavender accent.
seatd
mesa
libxkbcommon
xkeyboard-config
fontconfig
ttf-dejavu
ttf-jetbrains-mono
labwc
sway
hyprland
xorg-xwayland
waybar
wofi
foot
swaybg
swaylock
swayidle
mako
grim
slurp
wl-clipboard
polkit
pipewire
pipewire-pulse
pipewire-alsa
wireplumber

# --- power efficiency (longer battery: TLP + thermald) + firewall ---
tlp
thermald
cpupower
ufw

# --- boot + install (BIOS+UEFI live, GRUB dual-boot on installed systems) ---
efibootmgr
grub
os-prober
ntfs-3g
dosfstools
mtools
parted
gptfdisk
syslinux
mkinitcpio
mkinitcpio-archiso
archinstall
